  "body": "## What changed\n\nAI Chat can save, replace, remove, and test a provider API key.\nIt uses the existing OS keychain entries and environment-first lookup.\nThe entry field clears after save, cancel, and provider changes.\nThe panel never draws a stored key.\n\nThe panel checks cloud readiness when the provider or offline setting changes.\nEditing a cloud Model does not read the keychain again.\nOllama Model edits wait for a 500 ms pause before one readiness check.\nA cloud Model edit after a finished Test replaces the Test result with \"Model changed. Click Test to test this model.\"\nThe settings code reads `camcraft_app::clock::Instant`, because the std clock panics in the browser build.\nThe status names a missing key, an unavailable Ollama server, or a missing model.\nReady means that a key was found. It does not prove that the provider accepted it.\nTest sends a small request to the selected model. The provider can bill this request.\nCredential and network work runs in the background.\n\nThe setup help and guide explain keys, billing, OS permission prompts, and Ollama setup.\nThey include `ollama serve`, server check commands, `OLLAMA_HOST`, `OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH`, and `OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE`.\nThey state that a Gemini app subscription does not include an API key.\nThe help states the current endpoint limit.\nRemove deletes the stored key only. It does not revoke a key or remove an environment variable.\n\nEffort: medium\n\n## Remaining work\n\nThis PR supplies part of #3781. It does not close that issue.\n\n- #3803 tracks the ignored `live-ai` smoke tests for all providers, including key lookup, Ready, text, and `get_job`.\n- #3804 tracks a distinct key-rejected status for a wrong key.\n\nThe reporter's macOS hand-test waits until the live lane in #3803 runs.\nKeep this PR a draft while that requirement remains open.\n\nAfter that lane runs, use this checklist:\n\n1. Open View > Panels > AI Chat. Choose a cloud provider. Check its key and billing links.\n2. Save a key. Confirm that the entry clears and the status names the key source.\n3. If macOS asks, enter the login keychain password in its prompt. Choose Always Allow. Select Test.\n4. Send a read-only greeting. Replace the key and test again. Remove it and check the status.\n5. Check the other cloud help. Select Ollama and check its server and Model status.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThese immutable images are from the initial implementation. They show the key controls and use a fake credential backend.\nThey contain no actual key. The help text added in this review round needs a refreshed screenshot: capture was attempted, but the GPU renderer returned `No adapter found` (`CustomNativeAdapterSelectionError`). This host cannot render the updated help views.\n\nBefore:\n\n![AI Chat before the change](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/5c3d533bff3c5010be6abe2074c95bf3734044ad/issue-3781-ai-key-setup/before.png)\n\nAfter:\n\n![AI Chat after the change](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/5c3d533bff3c5010be6abe2074c95bf3734044ad/issue-3781-ai-key-setup/after.png)\n\nKey editor:\n\n![AI Chat key editor](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/5c3d533bff3c5010be6abe2074c95bf3734044ad/issue-3781-ai-key-setup/editor.png)\n\nReady state:\n\n![AI Chat ready state](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/5c3d533bff3c5010be6abe2074c95bf3734044ad/issue-3781-ai-key-setup/ready.png)\n\n## Validation\n\nFinal head: `1afd60cf48d1252c6e2b3aaa637f33b6f0f74c1c`.\nBase: current upstream/main `1a4c69d06f7365f07d94eca1fcbbe92605f077b9`.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: GREEN on the final head: 10/10 steps, 0 failed. UI lib: 1,556 passed, 0 failed, eight ignored. All eight integration suites passed. All 19 settings tests passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed on the final head, exit code 0, no warnings.\n- On head `e207e2355` (the last commit changes two `crates/ui` files only): `cargo xtask gate batch --only \"app suites: example_catalog\"`: passed, 1/1 step; 39 tests passed, four ignored.\n- `python3 -m unittest discover -s site/tests -p test_ai_guide.py`: passed, 4 tests.\n- Additional affected guide suites: `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test ai_guide`: 3 passed; `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test mcp_doc_drift`: 6 passed; `python3 -m unittest discover -s site/tests -p test_guide_refresh.py`: 14 passed.\n\nThe review-round pins count backend calls during Model edits and check the visible setup instructions.\nThey also cover explicit Test, queued checks, and Model edits during an in-flight cloud request.\n\n- Cloud Model editing: `cloud_model_edits_do_not_read_credentials_again_and_test_uses_latest_model`.\n- Ollama Model editing: `ollama_model_edits_check_once_after_the_last_keystroke_pause`.\n- Panel help: `provider_help_explains_ollama_options_and_gemini_subscription`.\n- Guide help: `test_provider_setup_explains_ollama_options_and_gemini_subscription`.\n\nMutation proof on this round: six source mutations each failed one named pin: remove the new help, restore cloud checks on Model edits, bypass the Ollama debounce, draw a stale local result, retain the queued check after explicit Test, and accept the old-model cloud Test result. Restored source passed all 17 settings tests. Removing the guide additions failed nine instruction checks; the restored guide passed all four tests.\n\nReview round 3 (review of `e207e2355`):\n\n- Clock seam: `ai_chat_sources_read_the_clock_seam_not_std_instant` scans each non-test file of `crates/ui/src/egui_app/ai_chat/`. It fails on a line that names `std::time` and `Instant`. Mutation: `use std::time::Instant;` in `settings.rs` made it fail (`settings.rs:8`). The restored code passed.\n- Stale Test result: `cloud_model_edit_after_a_finished_test_asks_for_a_new_test`. Mutation: the new status branch disabled made it fail (status stayed \"Ready\"). The restored code passed.\n- Restored source passed 19 of 19 settings tests.\n\nThe initial implementation also pins key save, replacement, removal, secret clearing, environment precedence, offline refusal, and stale-result handling.\nThe initial panel pin failed before the controls were added.\n\nHeavy lanes do not apply. The diff touches UI and guide code only.\nIt changes no app operations, motion, simulation, post, or geometry code.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The example catalog passed. The diff for `*.nc`, `*.cl`, and `examples/catalog/**` is empty. No program regeneration was needed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe reporter's macOS hand-test waits for #3803.\nReal OS keychain access, live cloud requests, and a live Ollama server were not exercised in this round.\nWindows, Linux, wasm, and the guide site render were not exercised. No wasm32 build ran: the clock fix is pinned by a source scan.\nStructural tests use a fake credential backend. Clippy builds the native HTTP code.\nRefreshed help screenshots could not be captured because this host has no usable GPU adapter. The visible help text is checked by structural UI tests.\n\nNo screenshot, log, or review evidence is committed to the source branch.\nImages belong only on the fork's `pr-screenshots` branch.\n\nChangelog: Add API key setup, provider readiness, and setup help to AI Chat.\n\nRefs #3781\n\n",
